name o3-01-unopposed-1
timeout 300
time 1973-10-06T12:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O3, SORTIE 1 OF 10 - YOM KIPPUR 1973: GROUND ATTACK IN CONTESTED AIRSPACE.
# THE BLOCKING MISSION, AND IT NO LONGER BLOCKS. THIS FILE IS THE CONTROL OF o3-02-command-post.fbm.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it IS the control, of 02.
#
# WHY THIS CAMPAIGN EXISTS AND WHY IT COULD NOT BE FLOWN UNTIL 2026-07-30. O3's own spec called itself
# "the only campaign in the set with zero runnable missions", blocked at the MODULE: `set task attack`
# was closed on `mig29` because the 9-12's unguided delivery is a DIRECTOR the pilot flies and not a
# release cue he reacts to, so `FBMig29FireControl` published no CCIP/CCRP block and the attack phase
# had no cue to pickle on. Gap C9 CLOSED 2026-07-30 (`core/FBDirector.h`,
# `modules/mig29/FBMig29Director.*`), and it was closed as a DIRECTOR: the aircraft picks the release
# moment, the pilot flies an instruction. The acceptance was the one measurement that would have caught
# a shortcut - same geometry, same fab500 on both sides, F-16 CCRP 34.02 m against MiG-29 OPT 65.65 m,
# a factor of 1.93 (`missions/mig29-opt-low.fbm`). A director that BEAT the computer would have been the
# F-16's procedure with Cyrillic labels.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION, stated in every file of this campaign because a reader who skips
# it reads every result backwards. The opening strikes of 6 October 1973 were flown by MiG-17, Su-7,
# Su-20, MiG-21 and Hawker Hunter [T4]; the MiG-29 entered service a decade later. Those five types are
# rows in `doc/modules/air/catalogue.md` and EVERY ONE OF THEM IS `ALPHA` - `make -C sim test-air` puts
# 10 of 10 generated decks outside their own acceptance bands - and an ALPHA row may not answer a
# campaign question. O3 therefore flies NO CATALOGUE ROW AT ALL and substitutes the `mig29` module for
# the period fighter-bomber, exactly as W3 and W4 did for their own casts.
#   DIRECTION: the MiG-29 makes the ATTACKER materially STRONGER than history - a supersonic
#   fourth-generation fighter with a look-down radar, an infrared search set and a modern warning
#   receiver, standing in for subsonic and first-generation supersonic attack aircraft. It is the
#   largest substitution in the whole ten-campaign set.
#   CONSEQUENCE FOR EVERY READING: an O3 result that still comes out BADLY says something STRONGER than
#   the record did. One that comes out well says nothing at all about 1973.
# The Israeli side is the `f16` module (the real defenders flew F-4, Mirage and A-4) - and where an
# Israeli fighter appears in this campaign it also makes BLUE stronger than history.
#
# THE ARENA, and every coordinate in it is [SET]. The Suez Canal sector, ~30.4-31.2 N 32.2-32.6 E
# [T4, approximate - the campaign file says so and this round does not improve on it]. Flown under
# `--elev const` on a 0 m datum (the real Sinai here is 0-60 m) and with NO TERRAIN MASKING (gap C4).
# Attack axis WEST -> EAST, because that is the direction the Egyptian strike crossed the canal.
#   the aim point   30.80000 32.62000 - a divisional artillery position east of the canal
#   the striker     spawns 6.02 km west of it at 300 m and 450 kt, egresses WEST across the canal
# Scale: 1 deg of latitude = 111 132 m; 1 deg of longitude at 30.80 N = 111 320 * cos(30.80 deg) =
# 95 619 m [DERIVED].
#
# WHY 300 M AND WHY A 6 KM FINAL - both are DERIVED from documented numbers and neither is taste.
#   ALTITUDE: the OPT director must range the target with the KOLS laser (reach 6 km, doc/sensors.md
#     §6) a lead time BEFORE the release point, and the release point sits one bomb-throw short of the
#     target. The throw grows with altitude, so the reach caps the level-delivery ALTITUDE. MEASURED
#     (`missions/mig29-opt-refused.fbm`): at 2 000 m the director still releases, at 2 200 m it returns
#     `DIRECTOR_REFUSED reason=no_release_point` and nothing leaves the jet. THE LEVEL-BOMBING CEILING
#     OF THIS AIRFRAME IS BETWEEN 2.0 AND 2.2 KM ASL. O3's anchor sentence - "Su-7 and MiG-17
#     fighter-bombers came in very low" [T1, Marine Corps study] - therefore falls out of one
#     documented rangefinder number rather than out of a mission author's preference.
#   FINAL LEG: this airframe's yaw channel is measured OFF (doc/modules/mig29/module.md gap 4i) and it
#     acquires a standing cross-track offset that saturates near 90-100 m within the first ~10 km of any
#     leg. A FAB-500 finishes a `target_soft` out to 68.4 m [DERIVED, below], so a long run-in cannot
#     hit at all. Sortie 03 measures that on a three-point ladder on THIS arena and publishes the
#     number; every other O3 striker therefore spawns on a ~6 km final, and it is declared here rather
#     than presented as doctrine.
#
# THE LETHAL RADIUS THAT DECIDES EVERY O3 VERDICT, derived once for the whole campaign from the tree's
# own damage model (`core/FBDamageModel.cpp` + `modules/ground/FBGroundTarget.h`, no new number):
#   flux(J/m^2) = 0.5 * (WarheadKg * 0.5 / (4*pi*r^2)) * (1800^2 + closure^2)
#   FAB-500, WarheadKg 201, closure ~214 m/s: `target_soft` fails (2.8e3 J/m^2) out to 68.4 m,
#   `target_hard` (9.0e4) out to 12.1 m. Plus the target's own 10 m / 6 m zone half-length along its
#   declared heading. FAB-250 (100 kg) reaches 48.3 m soft and 8.5 m hard [DERIVED].
# THE DIRECTOR DELIVERS AT 45-70 m. So a soft position is killable and a HARDENED one is not, and
# sortie 02 is that statement with a number instead of an argument.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: CAN THIS MODULE PLACE AN UNGUIDED STORE ON A DEFENDED-CLASS GROUND
# POSITION AT ALL, AND AT WHAT COST IN METRES? Nothing shoots at it here - no umbrella, no fighters, no
# AAA - because the campaign needs the delivery error of a clean pass as the reference every other
# sortie is read against. This is the sortie O3's spec called "the acceptance test for the
# director-mode work".
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, --elev const, campaign step 1, fingerprint cc5682956b788fc9, exit 0):
#   director   `LRF_RANGE` slantM 3 624.9 (inside the device's 6 km reach) at t = 10.4; consent 3.1 s
#              later (inside the documented 1...10 s window); `DIRECTOR_ARM` countdownS 4.347,
#              cmdG 1.000, planMissM 48.78; `DIRECTOR_RELEASE` meanGErr 0.043, maxBankDeg 0.912,
#              trackedS 4.3, openLoopAlongM -70.33 m, devSpeedMs -1.476
#   delivery   predErrM 45.57 m  aimErrM 66.39 m (long -45.52, across +48.34), tofS 8.20
#   the position DESTROYED at t = 26.2 by a single FAB-500 arriving 59.89 m from its centre
#              (fluxJm2 3 662.9 against the 2 800 threshold) - i.e. inside the 68.4 m derived radius
#              WITH 8.5 M TO SPARE. THAT MARGIN IS THIS CAMPAIGN'S WHOLE TOLERANCE and every sortie
#              below is read against it.
#   THE -70.33 M IS THE DIRECTOR'S OWN COST and it is the largest in the campaign, for the reason
#              sortie 03 measures: a 6 km final gives the plan only 4.3 s of stabilised flight to be
#              frozen from, and 1.476 m/s of airspeed the plan never knew about becomes 70 m of range.
#   sun elevation at spawn 40.55 deg (`mission CLOCK`), so the eye and every optical sight in this
#              campaign work: 14:00 local = 12:00 Z at UTC+2 [DERIVED], the anchor's own launch time.
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 = SUCCESS and it is binding here - `objective kill unit y1art` plus `survive`,
# so a run in which the director does not deliver, or delivers outside the derived radius, is a FAIL
# and says so. THE MEASUREMENT is the `director DIRECTOR_RELEASE` line and the `stores DELIVERY` line
# beside it. exit 1 would mean the position lived; exit 2 would be a defect.

unit y1str
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.55700 300 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off                  # a striker does not radiate: the one thing this jet must not do
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500                     # the mirror station - one pass, one store (weapons.md §5.4.5)
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt                    # the ONLY value this airframe accepts
  wp 30.80000 32.62000 300 450           # THE AIM POINT: the active steerpoint IS the target
  wp 30.86000 32.30000 300 450           # egress WEST, back across the canal
  wp 30.86000 32.15000 400 400
  objective kill unit y1art
  objective survive

unit y1art
  module target_soft                     # a divisional artillery position: unprotected, no FDM
  team friendly
  spawn 30.80000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0
